15:["$","$L44",null,{"children":[["$","$L45",null,{"title":"My outputs corrupt with --disk_cache","id":"my-outputs-corrupt-with---disk_cache","children":["$","p",null,{"children":["Bazel 9.1.0 has a client bug that corrupts outputs when the chunking flag is\ncombined with ",["$","code",null,{"children":"--disk_cache"}],". Use 9.1.1+ or 8.7.0+."]}]}],["$","$L45",null,{"title":"Clients never use chunking","id":"clients-never-use-chunking","children":["$","p",null,{"children":["Support is advertised through the capabilities service, so the instance needs a\n",["$","code",null,{"children":"capabilities"}]," entry. Check the client version too: the flag exists only from\nBazel 9.1.1 / 8.7.0."]}]}],["$","$L45",null,{"title":"Nothing gets chunked","id":"nothing-gets-chunked","children":["$","p",null,{"children":["Clients do not chunk blobs below the maximum chunk size, 4x\n",["$","code",null,{"children":"avg_chunk_size_bytes"}],". At the 512 KiB default that's everything under 2 MiB.\nBlobs producing more chunks than ",["$","code",null,{"children":"max_chunk_count"}]," are also served whole:\n",["$","code",null,{"children":"SplitBlob"}]," answers ",["$","code",null,{"children":"NOT_FOUND"}]," and the client downloads normally."]}]}],["$","$L45",null,{"title":"Errors from the chunk index store","id":"errors-from-the-chunk-index-store","children":["$","p",null,{"children":["It must not be the CAS store, and must not sit under ",["$","code",null,{"children":"verify"}],", because the layouts it\nholds are not content-addressed, so digest verification rejects them. Give it\nits own plain ",["$","code",null,{"children":"filesystem"}]," store."]}]}],["$","$L45",null,{"title":"Do I need to change anything for existing clients?","id":"do-i-need-to-change-anything-for-existing-clients","children":["$","p",null,{"children":"No. Chunking is opt-in and advertised through the capabilities service, so\nclients that don't request it (or predate it) keep using regular transfers\nagainst the same CAS."}]}],["$","$L45",null,{"title":"Chunking or wire compression?","id":"chunking-or-wire-compression","children":["$","p",null,{"children":["They solve different transfer problems. Chunking re-transfers only the changed\nparts of large, incrementally-changing blobs;\n",["$","$L6",null,{"href":"/how-to/stores/compression","children":"wire compression"}]," shrinks compressible blobs\nwholesale. Compressed artifacts chunk poorly (everything after the first\nchanged byte re-transfers), so lean on chunking for archives, binaries, and\nlayers, and on compression for text-heavy outputs."]}]}]]}]
